        ":question/id": "01d4210c-99cb-5509-8003-8615f9f2d644",
        ":question/problem": "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{3a-3b=-18; -2a+b=7$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=7+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-3b & =-18 \\\\ 3a-3(7+2a) & =-18 \\\\ 3a-21-6a & =-18 \\\\ -3a-21 & =-18 \\\\ -3a & =3 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=7+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7+2(-1) \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(5)=-6.$"
      },
      "role": "independently authored inventory",
      "relationship_to_source_templates": "Previously generated substitution instance; retained as raw inventory, excluded from observed template counts."
