        ":question/id": "76c476e0-406c-5751-a806-f5cbe03fe610",
        ":question/problem": "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{-3x+4y=8; -2x+y=6$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ y & =6+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=6+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y & =8 \\\\ -3x+4(6+2x) & =8 \\\\ -3x+24+8x & =8 \\\\ 5x+24 & =8 \\\\ 5x & =-16 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{16}{5}$ into $y=6+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6+2(-\\frac{16}{5}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{16}{5},\\,y=-\\frac{2}{5}.$"
      },
